* Layer and Cascade Strategy
By declaring layers, I can prevent specificity conflicts. Styles now flow logically.
Components are now modular. There are also print overrides.

* Custom Properties and Design Tokens
Reusing tokens in my design variables will heavily reduce duplication in my cod. Design tokens also work to make global design updates instantaneous. For example, if I want to alter a value, I can simply go to my :root and make changes that automatically change across all components that share the variables.

* Modularity

Clear naming makes components easy to plug into different parts of my HTML structure. Kind of like virtual legos. This makes the site maintainable.

* Browser Testing and Responsiveness

I tested layouts across different viewport widths to verify everything was adaptive. I also made sure that @media print functioned as intended and hid things like the navbar, buttons, etc.